 ### [Gaussian Splatting Rendering Pipeline](3415-gaussian-splatting-rendering-pipeline.md)
-The Gaussian Splatting Rendering Pipeline orchestrates camera setup, spherical harmonic (SH) evaluation, feature assembly, and Gaussian rasterization for a single view. It projects 3D Gaussians to 2D screen space, rasterizes them into tiles, and composites them front-to-back using alpha blending to produce novel views. It sets apart from its siblings by managing the pre-computation of covariances, colors, and lighting models, and assembling auxiliary features before invoking the differentiable rasterizer.
+The Gaussian Splatting Rendering Pipeline orchestrates the complete forward pass for generating a novel view from a set of trained 3D Gaussians. It converts raw Gaussian parameters (position, scale, rotation, opacity, spherical harmonics) into screen-space projections, evaluates view-dependent colors, and rasterizes the scene using alpha compositing. It differs from its siblings by providing the high-level orchestration and data assembly (camera setup, SH evaluation, feature concatenation) that wraps the core differentiable rasterization kernel.
 
 ### [Backpropagation with Per-Splat Parallelization](3533-backpropagation-with-per-splat-parallelization.md)
-This method is a parallelization scheme for the backward pass of 3D Gaussian Splatting rasterization that maps CUDA threads to 2D splats rather than pixels to eliminate atomic contention on gradient accumulation. It differs from the original 3DGS approach, which maps threads to pixels and suffers from serialized atomic operations when multiple threads contend for the same Gaussian's gradient, by having threads maintain per-splat state and exchange smaller per-pixel states (transmittance $T$ and accumulated color $RGB$) via intra-warp shuffling.
-
-### GaussianRasterizer Initialization and Input Validation
-Validates mutually exclusive input tensors for color representation and 3D covariance before invoking the CUDA rasterization backend [S1, unofficial]. It checks if exactly one of `shs` or `colors_precomp` is provided, and if exactly one of the scale/rotation pair or `cov3D_precomp` is provided [S1, unofficial]. If both are None or both are not None, it raises an exception [S1, unofficial]. It replaces any missing `shs`, `colors_precomp`, `scales`, `rotations`, or `cov3D_precomp` tensors with empty tensors of appropriate shape [S1, unofficial]. If `features` is None, it initializes it as an empty tensor matching the feature dimension of `means3D` (slice `[..., :0]`) [S1, unofficial]. It then calls the CUDA rasterization routine `rasterize_gaussians` with all prepared tensors and `raster_settings` [S1, unofficial].
